{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-10-36","kind":"proposition","title":"性质与证明：可公度量与二项无理线段与无理线段","englishTitle":"If two rational straight lines commensurable in square only be added together, the whole is irrational; and let it be called binomial.","book":10,"number":36,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.36","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.36/","group":"prop_1","sourceNumber":36,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-10-36@raw-6c097d0e91d3d569","contentId":"euclid-10-36","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"6c097d0e91d3d56973ad066b2184cd1518d22af8e573d9209e056ac678c2627f","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-10-36.statement","euclid-10-36.construction.1","euclid-10-36.proof.1","euclid-10-36.proof.2","euclid-10-36.proof.3","euclid-10-36.proof.4","euclid-10-36.proof.5","euclid-10-36.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-10-36.statement","contentId":"euclid-10-36","revisionId":"euclid-10-36@raw-6c097d0e91d3d569","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"888e19d8f21341021ea03c4c66581ec71f696ce82eda5b7d028b8c1f39eb3abe","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If two rational straight lines commensurable in square only be added together, the whole is irrational; and let it be called binomial."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果将两个有理线段 平方可公度而长度不可公度加在一起,则整个为无理;因此,这称为二项无理线段。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-36.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-10-36","revisionId":"euclid-10-36@raw-6c097d0e91d3d569","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"b0715d0afe0bb27a553c0ec2cb05189bbf2a4b33bdbb5fcab4e9ebe08241bfa2","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For let two rational straight lines AB, BC commensurable in square only be added together; I say that the whole AC is irrational."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"将2 有理线段 AB BC 平方可公度而长度不可公度加在一起;我说,整个AC是无理。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-36.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-10-36","revisionId":"euclid-10-36@raw-6c097d0e91d3d569","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"bb49d39a1c40e1f61c804610f94fc07e5b3f884cceb51bdb75000943d42c7a07","citations":["euclid-10-11"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, since AB is incommensurable in length with BC— for they are commensurable in square only— and, as AB is to BC, so is the rectangle AB, BC to the square on BC, therefore the rectangle AB, BC is incommensurable with the square on BC. [[X. 11](/principles/euclid-10-11) ]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因为AB的长度为不可公度,而AB的长度为AB,BC的长度为BC,矩形的长度为BC的长度为BC的长度为BC的长度为平方可公度而长度不可公度的长度为BC的长度为BC的长度,矩形的长度为BC的长度为正方形的长度为BC的长度为BC的长度为BC的长度为正方形的长度为BC的长度为BC的长度为BC的长度为9；上述对应量具有相同的比例关系。 [ [X. 11](/principles/euclid-10-11)"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-36.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-10-36","revisionId":"euclid-10-36@raw-6c097d0e91d3d569","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"98d9e1c996be7a6989d8793b90ba69e3ff3f1c91d38bc307493b16def726753b","citations":["euclid-10-6","euclid-10-15","euclid-10-13"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But twice the rectangle AB, BC is commensurable with the rectangle AB, BC [[X. 6](/principles/euclid-10-6) ], and the squares on AB, BC are commensurable with the square on BC—for AB, BC are rational straight lines commensurable in square only— [[X. 15](/principles/euclid-10-15) ] therefore twice the rectangle AB, BC is incommensurable with the squares on AB, BC. [[X. 13](/principles/euclid-10-13) ]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但是,矩形 AB,BC是可公度,矩形 AB,BC是可公度,AB,BC是正方形,BC是正方形,AB,BC是有理线段,平方可公度而长度不可公度,有理线段,平方可公度而长度不可公度 [ [ [ [X. 6](/principles/euclid-10-6) [X. 15](/principles/euclid-10-15) [X. 13](/principles/euclid-10-13)"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-36.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-10-36","revisionId":"euclid-10-36@raw-6c097d0e91d3d569","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"0d27748ef61656a547b01ada31690f874e533a578b356b33e8d3b58136e4e468","citations":["euclid-2-4","euclid-10-16"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And, componendo, twice the rectangle AB, BC together with the squares on AB, BC, that is, the square on AC [[II. 4](/principles/euclid-2-4) ], is incommensurable with the sum of the squares on AB, BC. [[X. 16](/principles/euclid-10-16) ]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"和, 兼容, 两倍的矩形 AB, BC 和正方形 AB, BC, 即, 正方形 AC], 和不可公度 和正方形 AB, BC [ [ [II. 4](/principles/euclid-2-4) [X. 16](/principles/euclid-10-16)"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-36.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-10-36","revisionId":"euclid-10-36@raw-6c097d0e91d3d569","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"af46eb37f5c6ef56fe6da589abc28274b2a78847527fdd0af328223270afe461","citations":["euclid-10-def-4"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But the sum of the squares on AB, BC is rational; therefore the square on AC is irrational, so that AC is also irrational. [[X. Def. 4](/principles/euclid-10-def-4) ]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但AB和BC的正方形和有理是有理,AC和正方形是无理,AC和正方形也是无理 [ [X. Def. 4](/principles/euclid-10-def-4)"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-36.proof.5","contentId":"euclid-10-36","revisionId":"euclid-10-36@raw-6c097d0e91d3d569","order":6,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 5","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"0e1e75e0788a6a0a9a817d0b18d290205ccb99caf260f03b3bc52a4698347658","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And let it be called binomial."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"让它被称为二项无理线段。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-36.source","contentId":"euclid-10-36","revisionId":"euclid-10-36@raw-6c097d0e91d3d569","order":7,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"e9cb7907561964c56a5bb30b47876736b5bb962153205bdbbfe29600ff9ee13a","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.36/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.36\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-10-36:euclid-10-11:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-10-36","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-10-36.proof.1"],"targetContentId":"euclid-10-11","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.36","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop